,"m":531},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_532","t":"Mrgerry\n\nI would like to share this chart on audusd Price is now CPing on old FTR area, which has engulfed. So I'm waiting retest and FTB on FL at this area to go long. I marked some other engulfing-games My thought and rules on S/D trading are really simples: a) Every time a level has engulfed, price pullback to fill the order, so I don't trade a level breakout b) a lot of time BB clear the stop having liquidity to shoot the price at best level to fill order c) until a strong level (FTR or resistance/supportl has not engulfed, price will go to next level, according on the previous trend d) I entry with FTB to FL if FL is over or before a level engulfed, not after e) When I watch a CP, I guess there is an important level. And I wait to catch the correct one\n\nThere are other things I've never understood 1) which is the correct origin of a pole, how mark the correct one 2) how mark correct PAZ with time and studiyng and community all will become clear","a":"—","d":"","n":"#532","p":22,"im":["ed9dff18ebc0d53dba7ac56e1bc015aa57697a8f"],"m":532},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_533","t":"Ezio\n\nOk Harry I scrapped that last chart and went back into the FL homework section reading many posts. Take a look at this chart I think I may have it now. If so Its starting to make more sense. I caught a reply of yours stating \" mark your S and R levels and you shall see FL's forming from them \". And that's how I spotted this one. Feel free to criticize as needed.\n\nTraining","a":"—","d":"","n":"#533","p":22,"im":["1e12b0a6bc9e83614d52d4624149668c426d347d"],"m":533},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_534","t":"Will be studying Flag Limits in earnest this week. For now, a quick query. I've marked what might possibly be a FL. Would appreciate a quick Yes//No. Thanks.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#534","p":22,"im":["9390e3aea16ef67e7c1289c0c3899952f3febf80"],"m":534},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_535","t":"Hi, My thoughts:","a":"—","d":"","n":"#535","p":22,"im":["b6218d1be558