R and therefore is not a FL. In my opinion, this is a DBR/Decision Point. And it is a very significant one at that. The Key SR level marked in the previous chart is actually the previous all time high for the S&P 500 market. The DBR is the decision to break that high. And that demand survived SIX attempts by the sellers before giving away (not shown in my chart). That's what I see anyway.\n\nGJ.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#543","p":22,"im":["a56bae86311e61d6e0239d257b2799a56f8fce5b","7180eaf69dd6d093684c4a77b9964f68868cffe9"],"m":543},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_544","t":"Ezio\n\nThis chart is the EURUSD M5 Flag limit explaination. This comes from my EURUSD H1 chart up above showing the top FL. I'm trying to fully understand the flag limits and how to use them correctly. So more posting is definitely on the way.\n\nTraining","a":"—","d":"","n":"#544","p":22,"im":["c677837a404e741613abc1bbc5b0a888c1d762f1"],"m":544},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_545","t":"Ezio\n\nEURAUD H1 FL with FTB and bounce.\n\nEURAUD M5 FL Limits\n\nTraining","a":"—","d":"","n":"#545","p":22,"im":["cd18c9b596a43bf51177f1ab7d9f3414ecb405b2","25479bf29cd638cc9e5bfd0512e52fd2c30ac20f"],"m":545},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_546","t":"Ezio\n\nEURAUD FL LIMIT REACTIONS: On my EurAud M5 FL chart above I drew in a yellow box around the flag limit areas. Did I do that right? If you look at this chart the candles aren't touching the actual FL the red boxed area. Though if the yellow box is correct those 2 areas both touch the flag limits perfectly. If that makes any sense..\n\nAny help would be super appreciated...meanwhile going to post some more charts\n\nTraining","a":"—","d":"","n":"#546","p":22,"im":["6f23cc277596f3346964ceb871db011445f6924e"],"m":546},{"id":"flaglimits_p22_547","t":"EURCAD FL M1 reaction.\n\nHow would you guy approach this if you ever take the trade? First of all, did I identify the FL correctly in both M15 and M1 TF. After seeing the FO, only then I goes down to M1 TF to find a reason for the reaction. Will